[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m123[m[36m-[m## Key design decisions in this layer
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m124[m[36m-[m
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m125[m[36m-[m**The secret code doesn't live as a hash for live verification.**
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m126[m[36m-[m`rounds.secret_code_hash` (from the data layer) is good for audit/
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m127[m[36m-[mdetecting corruption, but "does this AI response *contain* the code" is a
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m128[m[36m-[msubstring-match problem — you can't hash-compare your way through that.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m129[m[36m-[m`RoundSecretsProvider` is the abstraction: plaintext code lives outside
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m130[m[36m-[mthe main DB (a real secrets manager in production; `InMemorySecretsProvider`
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m131[m[36m-[mfor now), and `get_verified_code()` re-hashes it against the round's
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m132[m[36m-[mstored hash before trusting it — a `SecretMismatchError` on any drift
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m133[m[36m-[mbetween the two, rather than silently producing a wrong verdict.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m134[m[36m-[m
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m135[m[36m-[m**The round is only locked at the moment of claiming a win**, not across
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m136[m[36m-[mthe AI call. Holding a DB row lock for the duration of a slow external
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m137[m[36m-[mAPI call would serialize every attempt on a round through the AI's
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m138[m[36m-[mresponse latency — the exact opposite of what you want for a game meant
[35mREADME.md[m[36m:[m[32m139[m[36m:[mto be playable by multiple people. See `[1;31m_claim_win_or_lose_the_race[m` in
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m140[m[36m-[m`game_service.py`.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m141[m[36m-[m
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m142[m[36m-[m**Two independent mechanisms prevent a double win**, on purpose:
[35mREADME.md[m[36m:[m[32m143[m[36m:[m1. The row lock + status check in `[1;31m_claim_win_or_lose_the_race[m`, which is
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m144[m[36m-[m   what makes the *loser* of a race fail gracefully into
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m145[m[36m-[m   `LOST_ROUND_CLOSED` instead of an ugly error.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m146[m[36m-[m2. The partial unique index from the data layer, as a backstop if the
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m147[m[36m-[m   lock is ever weaker than expected (e.g. isolation-level surprises).
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m148[m[36m-[m   `test_genuine_race_is_caught_by_the_index_backstop` forces this path
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m149[m[36m-[m   directly and confirms it degrades cleanly rather than crashing.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m150[m[36m-[m
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m151[m[36m-[m**Every state transition is retryable from where it failed.**
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m152[m[36m-[m`AI_REQUEST_FAILED` and `PAYOUT_FAILED` are real, queryable states — a
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m153[m[36m-[mbackground worker (not built yet) would poll for
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m154[m[36m-[m`ATTEMPT_ACTIONABLE_STATUSES` and call `retry_ai_call` / `retry_payout`.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m155[m[36m-[mRetrying never re-charges the player or creates a second AI/payout row —
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m156[m[36m-[msame message, same payout, tried again.
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m157[m[36m-[m
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m158[m[36m-[m**A player who paid before round closure still gets their AI response.**
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m159[m[36m-[mIf their message happens to match the code but the round already closed
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m160[m[36m-[min the meantime, they're marked `LOST_ROUND_CLOSED` — not silently
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m161[m[36m-[mdropped, and not billed twice to find out. See
[35mREADME.md[m[36m-[m[32m162[m[36m-[m`test_second_winning_message_after_round_already_closed`.
